  "strDescriptionEN": "Abraham Jeriel Richard Dorsett (born 4 May 2002) is a professional footballer who plays as a defender for Reading. Born in England, he plays for the Montserrat national team.\r\n\r\nCareer\r\nOn 21 October 2019, Dorsett signed his first professional contract with Reading. Dorsett made his professional debut with Reading in a 1-0 FA Cup loss to Luton Town F.C. on 9 January 2021.\r\n\r\nOn 20 August 2021, Dorsett joined Rochdale on a season long loan. He was then loaned to Kilmarnock in August 2022.\r\n\r\nOn 11 July 2023, Dorsett signed a new one-year contract with the club, until the summer of 2024.\r\n\r\nInternational career\r\nDorsett represented England at U17 and U18 level. \r\n\r\nDorsett was called up to the Montserrat senior squad for the first time in September 2023, for their matches in the 2023\u201324 CONCACAF Nations League B against Barbados and Dominican Republic.",
